# Drone mode naming

The third drone state enum is **`THE_LAST_OF_2028`**, not `LAST_OF_2028` and not any `TEST_OF_*` variant.
User-facing matrix / scroll text is **`THE LAST OF EE2028`** (with the leading `THE`).

## Required names

| Kind | Correct | Forbidden |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Enum / state | `THE_LAST_OF_2028` | `LAST_OF_2028`, `TEST_OF_2028`, `TEST_OF_EE2028`, `TEST_OF_EE_2028`, `THE_LAST_OF_EE2028` |
| Handler | `Handle_The_Last_Of_2028_Mode` | `Handle_Last_Of_2028_Mode`, `Handle_EE2028_Mode`, `Handle_Test_Of_*` |
| Event (if used) | `DRONE_EVENT_ENTER_THE_LAST_OF_2028` | `DRONE_EVENT_ENTER_LAST_OF_2028` |
| Matrix / display banner | `THE LAST OF EE2028` | `LAST OF EE2028`, `LAST OF 2028`, `TEST OF EE2028` |
| Prose / docs | "The Last of EE2028" | "Last of 2028", "Test of EE2028", "Test of 2028" |

## Examples

```c
// ❌ BAD
case LAST_OF_2028:
case TEST_OF_EE2028:
case THE_LAST_OF_EE2028:
    Handle_Last_Of_2028_Mode();
static const char kLastText[] = "LAST OF EE2028";

// ✅ GOOD
case THE_LAST_OF_2028:
    Handle_The_Last_Of_2028_Mode();
static const char kLastText[] = "THE LAST OF EE2028";
```

If you see a forbidden name in a diff or existing file, rename it to the correct form before finishing the task.
